{"name":"Falcon","hex":"#6e5a5b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Falcon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.\nA surname from Spanish.\nA surname, from Native Indigenous Amerindian languages.","A surname from Spanish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Falcon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Falcon","blocks":[{"text":"Falcons are birds of prey in the genus Falco, which includes about 40 species. Some small species of falcons with long, narrow wings are called hobbies, and some that hover while hunting are called kestrels. Falcons are widely distributed on all continents of the world except Antarctica, though closely related raptors did occur there in the Eocene."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Eurasian_hobby_%28Falco_subbuteo%29_by_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg/330px-Eurasian_hobby_%28Falco_subbuteo%29_by_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falcon","wikidata":"Q43489"},{"title":"Falcon (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"The Falcon is a superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The character was introduced by writer-editor Stan Lee and artist Gene Colan in Captain America #117."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Falcon_%28Samuel_Thomas_%22Sam%22_Wilson%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falcon_(comics)","wikidata":"Q672591"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/FalconHeadBeak.png/330px-FalconHeadBeak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/FalconHeadBeak.png/330px-FalconHeadBeak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Most members of the genus Falco show a \"tooth\" on the upp